sections.wikitext:
{{Listen
 |pos          = left
 |filename     = Goodies.ogg
 |title="Goodies"
 |description="Goodies," the [[crunk]] counterpart to "[[Yeah! (Usher song)|Yeah!]]," lyrically speaks of female empowerment and [[abstinence]]-promoting lyrics.
}}

"Goodies" drew comparisons to the Usher song "Yeah!" and [[Kelis]]'s "[[Milkshake (song)|Milkshake]]."<ref name="slant">{{cite web|url=http://www.slantmagazine.com/music/review/ciara-goodies/496|title=Ciara: Goodies – Music Review|work=[[Slant Magazine]]|access-date=July 21, 2010|date=September 4, 2004|first=Sal|last=Cinquemani}}</ref> The song makes use of a repeated whistle, "faux [[Opera|operatic]] vocals" in parts, and a [[Western music (North America)|western]] guitar riff near the end.<ref name="slant" />
"Goodies" is a midtempo [[Contemporary R&B|crunk&B]] song. The song features a whistling beat, with several crunk-[[Pop music|pop]] synths throughout its course, and a guitar rhythm as it opens into its third verse and in its outro. Petey Pablo raps the first part of the first and third verses, while Ciara sings the rest of the song.
{{Clear}}

